{"baseRefName":"fix/interaction-trust","baseRefOid":"4d36ee2926ee1b098ec35eede3e16773e7c0847e","body":"## Summary\n\nAudit-hardening batch on top of #528 — closes the network-trust gaps the\nmulti-agent review found in provider fetch/curl/HLS paths:\n\n- **Bounded DNS** — `resolvedAddressBlockReason` raced resolver answers\n  against nothing; a dead resolver hung SSRF validation indefinitely.\n  4s shared budget (unref'd), caller `AbortSignal` honored, errors return\n  \"no addresses\" so the real fetch keeps its own failure path.\n- **Bounded bodies** — `shared/bounded-body.ts` caps provider response\n  text/bytes at 8 MiB and playlists at 2 MiB; `null` means over-cap or\n  read failure while prefix readers return partial bytes. Applied to the\n  shared transport, stream-reachability, HLS ladder, movy seed/ciphertext\n  reads, anime metadata, DownloadService subtitle reads, and the offline\n  artwork cache.\n- **Per-hop curl redirects** — `curl -sL` followed up to 50 hops with\n  zero validation. Rewritten as an in-process walk: each `Location` is\n  scheme-checked, HTTPS-downgrade rejected, literal+DNS blocklisted,\n  cross-origin sensitive headers stripped, 4-hop ceiling. Bare-fetch\n  fallback routes through `createGuardedFetch`.\n- **Bounded concurrency** — Rivestream source/HLS expansion capped at\n  4 workers; VidLink backoff sleeps are abort-aware.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `blocked-target.test.ts` — bounded DNS (15ms seam), abort, private\n      answers\n- [x] `provider-http-transport.test.ts` — per-hop curl walk, private /\n      non-HTTP / downgrade rejection, header stripping, hop ceiling,\n      over-cap stdout\n- [x] `stream-reachability.test.ts` — Range-ignoring segment probe reads\n      only the prefix; oversized playlist rejected\n- [x] Focused suites: 168 pass / 0 fail; anti-slop baseline green\n      (4407, safety-comment ratcheted to 1813)\n\nStacked on #528.","files":[{"path":"apps/cli/src/infra/net/guarded-remote-fetch.ts","additions":7,"deleti